{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's record may not be used to build the case against her. Her 3 prior_no_show_flags is a LIFETIME counter and is not the rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d that POL-NS-09(d) reads; the trailing-30-day figure on this profile is 1, far below the threshold of 3, so no abuse escalation arises out of her side of the file. Under POL-GEN-01 her rating (4.66), account_age_days (1830), lifetime_trips (1290), cancellation_rate (0.071), prior_disputes_filed (4) and prior_disputes_upheld (1) are CONTEXT ONLY: they may inform how closely her assertions are scrutinised and may never ground or carry an adverse finding about this trip. The only rider field citable on a no-show question is no_show_disputes_30d, and it does not support a finding against her.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-00208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-01", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I do not put POL-NS-04, and I say so rather than stretch it. The rider did send a coordinating message inside the waiting window ('coming coming 2 min', sent 16:08:02, read 16:08:11), but limb (b) fails on the driver's side of the record: he replied 'ok no problem' at 16:08:20, eighteen seconds later, and placed an in-app call that was answered for 34 seconds at 16:09:40, both before he terminated the trip. Limb (c) fails on the rider's own track, which records 0 qualifying fixes inside the 150 m rider_presence_radius_m for this LARGE_VENUE zone. On this record the rider-contact clause cannot be made out.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00208", "EV-TRIP-00208", "EV-GPS-00208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.rider_qualifying_fix_count",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The thing this record does not settle is where the rider was, and the two admissible artifacts that speak to it contradict each other directly. The chat log shows the rider telling the driver at 16:08:02 that she is 'coming coming 2 min' - an assertion that she was moving and moments away - while the rider's own track in the same window records 141 fixes from 15:54:00 to 16:15:20 at a single distinct speed of 0.0 kph and a mean distance of 639.8 m from the pickup pin: on the platform's own telemetry she never moved at all. No clause resolves which of the two is right; POL-NS-04(c) can only say she was outside the 150 m presence radius on admissible fixes, not whether she was on her way. I do not dispute that the driver's own hold of the guardhouse ran 585 seconds inside the arrival radius - my point is that the rider's side of the same event is unresolved on admissible artifacts, which is the POL-NS-09(b) situation of two artifacts in direct conflict on rider presence with no clause to settle it. That is also exactly what the rider asked for: somebody to call her about this. Escalated, the disputed $8.00 is held rather than collected under POL-GEN-03, which is the only outcome on this record that does not charge the rider on a question the platform cannot answer.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00208", "EV-GPS-00208", "EV-TRIP-00208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-04", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider never named a block, tower, bay or entrance: her only message in the window is 'coming coming 2 min', and POL-NS-03 is the clause that deals with a rider who is not at the labelled point but is not to blame for it - where neither party specified a sub-location and registered_pickup_points is 2 or more, it attributes the mislocation to pin ambiguity rather than to either party, and the platform-funded goodwill is never recovered from the rider. The trip record's own figures show a condominium pickup with 2 registered pickup points and a pin labelled 'Main Guardhouse', while the rider's track sits 633.9 to 646.4 m from that pin for the entire window. I accept that POL-NS-03's 120-to-400 m distance gate cannot itself be run here, because the driver's fixes fall inside the 120 m arrival radius, so the clause does not by its own terms produce the refund; I ask the Judge to record the pin ambiguity as the specific open question the reviewer must settle under POL-NS-09, because treating a 640 m gap between the platform's own pin and the platform's own rider track as the rider's fault is not something this record supports.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00208", "EV-GPS-00208", "EV-CHAT-00208"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03", "POL-NS-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.min_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 6.4,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 6.4,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: I have decided this on the platform's own records for TRP-00208, and they agree with one another.\n\nThe driver's side is established. The GPS trace runs unbroken at 10-second intervals, 100% coverage, no gap, and it places the driver at the main guardhouse inside the 120 m arrival radius for this condominium (LARGE_VENUE) pickup from 16:02:10, holding position in a single continuous run of 585 seconds until 16:11:55. The trip record carries the driver's 'arrived' event at 16:02:25 and the driver's cancellation at 16:12:10 on reason RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event. That satisfies all four conditions for a chargeable no-show: the arrival event exists; the trace puts the driver in the geofence before it (first qualifying fix 16:02:10, fifteen seconds before the marker); he held the geofence for at least the 300 seconds this zone class requires — he held it for 585 seconds, a surplus of 285 seconds; and the trip was terminated by the driver on the no-show code after the dwell had elapsed. The arrival marker is not false: the 16:02:25 event sits inside the same in-geofence run, with recorded speed 0.0 km/h and nothing putting the driver more than 300 m from the pin or in motion at the moment he marked arrival.\n\nThe fee is $8.00, not $4.00, because the charge is the greater of the LARGE_VENUE zone-class fee ($4.00) and the RYDE_XL vehicle-tier fee ($8.00), and the vehicle-tier figure is the higher.\n\nThe driver is therefore paid and the rider's refund request is not granted. Under the compensation clause the driver receives 80% of the $8.00 fee — $6.40 — with the remaining 20% ($1.60) retained as the platform's service fee. The anti-farming check does not withhold it: the driver has 2 no-show terminations in the last 30 days, below the threshold of 4, and 2 against 143 completed trips is a ratio of 0.014, well below the 0.08 limit.\n\nOn the rider's specific complaints: you say the driver never came and you could not reach him by phone. The records show otherwise. The driver placed an in-app call at 16:09:40 which was answered and ran 34 seconds, and every message he sent was delivered and read — his 16:02:40 message with his plate number (read at 16:03:01) and his 16:07:15 follow-up (read at 16:07:29). You replied 'coming coming 2 min' at 16:08:02 and he answered 'ok no problem' eighteen seconds later. Your own phone's location, meanwhile, recorded 141 fixes between 15:54:00 and 16:15:20, all at 0.0 km/h, at a mean of about 640 m from the pickup pin and never closer than about 634 m: the device stayed at the Block 5 lift lobby inside the estate and never entered the 150 m rider-presence radius around the pickup point. The account that you waited at the guardhouse is not supported by the telemetry.\n\nOn the request to escalate to a human reviewer, I have considered it and I decline it. The two records said to conflict do not: your chat message was a statement that you were on your way, not a claim of position, and it does not contradict a track showing you never moved; the rider-presence question is in any case answered by the clause that reads your track, which places you outside the presence radius on admissible fixes; and your presence is not what the no-show fee depends on. There is no direct conflict between admissible artifacts, no clock skew, no trace gap, no truncated chat and no fare mismatch — every record carrying a deciding fact here is complete at full weight. The one absent artifact, the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-00208-01 (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), carries no fact and is not needed. Every profile field either side raised as reputation — the rider's rating, account age, lifetime trips, cancellation and prior-dispute counts, and her lifetime no-show flags — is context only and has played no part in this outcome. Your wish to be called is noted; it is not something this ruling can order, and the underlying charge is correct as it stands."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
